{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261113T015009Z_dev-03_staged_8ce7", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "In Kim, Lee, Park and Shin (arXiv:1601.05089), the best fit for ψψ̄ → h2h2 used m_ψ = 69.2 GeV and m_h2 = 35.7 GeV. The annihilation cross section was ⟨σv⟩ = 2.26×10⁻²⁶ cm³ s⁻¹, with Ωh² = 0.121. The J-factor was rescaled to 𝒥 = 2.2 times the canonical value, i.e. J̄ = 2.2 × J̄_canonical, giving χ² = 23.19 (p = 0.39).", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "7.1"}]}, "turns": 11, "seconds": 22.139, "tool_calls": 12, "tool_result_chars": 55435, "input_tokens": 169333, "output_tokens": 1672, "parser_versions": ["3"], "ended_at": "2026-11-13T01:50:32+00:00"}
